{"text": "sixteen", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">sextene</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">sixtene</i>, from Old English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"ang\">sixt\u012bene</i>, from Proto-Germanic <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"gem-pro\">*sehstehun</i>. Cognate with West Frisian <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fy\">sechstjin</i>, Dutch <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"nl\">zestien</i>, German <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"de\">sechzehn</i>, Danish <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"da\">seksten</i>. Equivalent to <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">six</i> +\u200e <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">-teen</i>.\n</p>", "pos": []}], "pronunciation": [["UK, US", "/\u02c8s\u026aks.ti\u02d0n/"], ["UK, US", "/\u02ccs\u026aks\u02c8ti\u02d0n/"]]}